---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";
import Sidebar from "../components/sidebar.astro";
---

<Layout title="Family Promise | Glen Meredith">
    <div class="page-wrapper">
        <Sidebar currentPage="family-promise" />
        
        <div class="page-content">
            <div id="content">
                <!-- Hero Section -->
                <section class="hero-gradient text-white py-24 px-6">
                    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
                        <div class="mb-6">
                            <span
                                class="inline-block bg-white/20 backdrop-blur-sm px-4 py-2 rounded-full text-sm font-medium"
                            >
                                UX Research · Information Architecture · 5 Weeks
                            </span>
                        </div>
                        <h1
                            class="text-6xl md:text-7xl font-black mb-6 leading-tight"
                        >
                            Family Promise
                        </h1>
                        <p
                            class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-light max-w-2xl leading-relaxed opacity-90"
                        >
                            Using card sorting and data visualization to
                            transform a cluttered nonprofit website into a
                            clear, trust-building resource.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6">
                    <!-- Hero Image - Before/After Sitemap -->
                    <div class="scroll-reveal mb-24 -mt-16 relative z-10">
                        <div
                            class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-2xl overflow-hidden"
                        >
                            <img
                                src="/fp-hero.webp"
                                alt="Sitemap before and after redesign"
                                class="w-full"
                            />
                        </div>
                        <p
                            class="text-center text-gray-500 mt-6 text-sm uppercase tracking-wider"
                        >
                            19 Pages → 6 Main Sections
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Introduction -->
                    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-5 gap-12 mb-32 scroll-reveal">
                        <div class="md:col-span-3">
                            <h2 class="text-5xl font-black mb-8 leading-tight">
                                From Chaos to Clarity
                            </h2>
                            <div
                                class="space-y-6 text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"
                            >
                                <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900">
                                    Imagine trying to navigate a website where
                                    critical information is buried under layers
                                    of redundancy—where "Our Story" and "Our
                                    History" are separate pages, yet neither
                                    fully answers your questions.
                                </p>
                                <p>
                                    For Family Promise of Salt Lake, a nonprofit
                                    dedicated to supporting families
                                    experiencing homelessness, this was the
                                    reality. Their outdated, cluttered website
                                    risked undermining trust with the very
                                    people who needed them most: families in
                                    crisis, potential donors, and volunteers.
                                </p>
                                <p>
                                    As the sole UX researcher and designer for
                                    my senior capstone project, I led a 5-week
                                    initiative to redesign the organization's
                                    information architecture. With no direct
                                    access to end users, I turned to card
                                    sorting and custom data visualization to
                                    uncover how people intuitively organized the
                                    site's content.
                                </p>
                                <div
                                    class="bg-blue-50 border-l-4 border-blue-600 p-6 rounded-r-lg my-8"
                                >
                                    <p class="font-bold text-blue-900 mb-2">
                                        The Result
                                    </p>
                                    <p class="text-gray-700">
                                        A streamlined sitemap that reduced 19
                                        pages to 6 main sections, eliminated
                                        redundancy, and positioned Family
                                        Promise as the professional, trustworthy
                                        organization it truly is.
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="md:col-span-2">
                            <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
                                <h3
                                    class="text-sm uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-400 mb-6"
                                >
                                    Project Details
                                </h3>
                                <div class="space-y-6">
                                    <div>
                                        <p
                                            class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-400 mb-1"
                                        >
                                            Role
                                        </p><p class="text-xl font-bold">
                                            UX Researcher, Designer & PM
                                        </p>
                                    </div>
                                    <div>
                                        <p
                                            class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-400 mb-1"
                                        >
                                            Timeline
                                        </p><p class="text-xl font-bold">
                                            July–August 2025 (5 weeks)
                                        </p>
                                    </div>
                                    <div>
                                        <p
                                            class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-400 mb-1"
                                        >
                                            Team
                                        </p><p class="text-xl font-bold">
                                            Solo UX + Developer Partner
                                        </p>
                                    </div>
                                    <div>
                                        <p
                                            class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-400 mb-1"
                                        >
                                            Context
                                        </p><p class="text-xl font-bold">
                                            Senior Capstone Project
                                        </p>
                                    </div>
                                    <div>
                                        <p
                                            class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-400 mb-1"
                                        >
                                            Client
                                        </p><p class="text-xl font-bold">
                                            Family Promise of Salt Lake
                                        </p>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- The Problem -->
                    <div class="mb-32 scroll-reveal">
                        <h2
                            class="text-5xl md:text-6xl font-black mb-16 leading-tight"
                        >
                            The<br />Problem
                        </h2>

                        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 mb-12">
                            <div>
                                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">
                                    The Challenge
                                </h3>
                                <p
                                    class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-6"
                                >
                                    Family Promise of Salt Lake's website
                                    suffered from years of accumulated content
                                    without strategic oversight. The sitemap had
                                    ballooned to 19 pages filled with
                                    overlapping, outdated, and poorly organized
                                    information.
                                </p>
                            </div>
                            <div class="bg-red-50 rounded-xl p-8">
                                <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-red-900 mb-4">
                                    Key Issues
                                </h3>
                                <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-700">
                                    <li class="flex items-start">
                                        <span
                                            class="text-red-600 mr-2 font-bold"
                                            >•</span
                                        >
                                        <span
                                            ><strong>Redundancy:</strong> Multiple
                                            pages covered similar content ("Our Story,"
                                            "Our History," "About Us")</span
                                        >
                                    </li>
                                    <li class="flex items-start">
                                        <span
                                            class="text-red-600 mr-2 font-bold"
                                            >•</span
                                        >
                                        <span
                                            ><strong>Poor Hierarchy:</strong> Critical
                                            actions buried in submenus</span
                                        >
                                    </li>
                                    <li class="flex items-start">
                                        <span
                                            class="text-red-600 mr-2 font-bold"
                                            >•</span
                                        >
                                        <span
                                            ><strong>Unclear Structure:</strong> Users
                                            couldn't predict where to find information</span
                                        >
                                    </li>
                                    <li class="flex items-start">
                                        <span
                                            class="text-red-600 mr-2 font-bold"
                                            >•</span
                                        >
                                        <span
                                            ><strong>Trust Erosion:</strong> Cluttered
                                            navigation signaled disorganization</span
                                        >
                                    </li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div
                            class="bg-gradient-to-br from-blue-700 to-cyan-700 text-white rounded-2xl p-12 diagonal-section"
                        >
                            <div class="max-w-3xl">
                                <p
                                    class="text-sm uppercase tracking-wider mb-4 opacity-80"
                                >
                                    The Constraint
                                </p>
                                <p
                                    class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold leading-snug"
                                >
                                    Without direct access to the nonprofit's end
                                    users, I needed an objective,
                                    research-backed method to understand how
                                    people expected the site to be organized.
                                </p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- User Groups -->
                    <div class="mb-32 scroll-reveal">
                        <h2
                            class="text-5xl md:text-6xl font-black mb-16 leading-tight"
                        >
                            Who We're<br />Designing For
                        </h2>

                        <p
                            class="text-xl text-gray-700 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-12"
                        >
                            Before restructuring the site, I identified three
                            distinct user groups with different needs and goals:
                        </p>

                        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
                            <div
                                class="bg-white rounded-xl p-8 shadow-lg hover:shadow-xl transition-shadow"
                            >
                                <div class="text-4xl mb-4">👨‍👩‍👧</div>
                                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">
                                    Families in Crisis
                                </h3>
                                <div class="space-y-3 text-gray-700">
                                    <p>
                                        <strong>Primary Need:</strong> Fast access
                                        to "Get Help" resources
                                    </p>
                                    <p>
                                        <strong>Behavior:</strong> High-stress browsing,
                                        need immediate clarity
                                    </p>
                                    <p>
                                        <strong>Pain Point:</strong> Can't afford
                                        to hunt through menus when facing homelessness
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <div
                                class="bg-white rounded-xl p-8 shadow-lg hover:shadow-xl transition-shadow"
                            >
                                <div class="text-4xl mb-4">💰</div>
                                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">
                                    Potential Donors
                                </h3>
                                <div class="space-y-3 text-gray-700">
                                    <p>
                                        <strong>Primary Need:</strong> Verify legitimacy
                                        and understand impact
                                    </p>
                                    <p>
                                        <strong>Behavior:</strong> Looking for mission,
                                        financials, success stories
                                    </p>
                                    <p>
                                        <strong>Pain Point:</strong> Disorganized
                                        sites signal mismanagement, reduce donation
                                        likelihood
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <div
                                class="bg-white rounded-xl p-8 shadow-lg hover:shadow-xl transition-shadow"
                            >
                                <div class="text-4xl mb-4">🙋</div>
                                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">
                                    Volunteers
                                </h3>
                                <div class="space-y-3 text-gray-700">
                                    <p>
                                        <strong>Primary Need:</strong> Find opportunities
                                        and understand time commitments
                                    </p>
                                    <p>
                                        <strong>Behavior:</strong> Comparing multiple
                                        organizations, need clear info
                                    </p>
                                    <p>
                                        <strong>Pain Point:</strong> Vague or scattered
                                        volunteer info leads to drop-off
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="bg-blue-50 rounded-xl p-8 mt-12">
                            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">
                                Design Implication
                            </h3>
                            <p class="text-lg text-gray-700">
                                The sitemap needed to serve high-stress urgent
                                users AND leisurely research-oriented
                                users—requiring both prominent critical actions
                                and clear exploratory paths.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Research Process -->
                    <div class="mb-32 scroll-reveal">
                        <h2
                            class="text-5xl md:text-6xl font-black mb-16 leading-tight"
                        >
                            Research<br />Process
                        </h2>

                        <div class="mb-12">
                            <h3 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">
                                Why Card Sorting?
                            </h3>
                            <p
                                class="text-xl text-gray-700 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl"
                            >
                                Card sorting reveals users' mental models—how
                                they naturally group and categorize information.
                                Without access to Family Promise's actual users,
                                this method let me gather objective data about
                                information organization from representative
                                participants.
                            </p>
                        </div>

                        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 mb-12">
                            <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-8 shadow-lg">
                                <div
                                    class="text-3xl font-black number-badge mb-4"
                                >
                                    01
                                </div>
                                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">
                                    Content Extraction
                                </h3>
                                <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
                                    I audited the existing sitemap and extracted
                                    every topic, page name, and major content
                                    section. This became exactly <strong
                                        >20 individual "cards"</strong
                                    > in FigJam—each representing a discrete piece
                                    of information users might need.
                                </p>
                            </div>

                            <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-8 shadow-lg">
                                <div
                                    class="text-3xl font-black number-badge mb-4"
                                >
                                    02
                                </div>
                                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">
                                    Participant Recruitment
                                </h3>
                                <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                                    Recruited <strong>10 participants</strong> through
                                    personal networks and my developer partner Matthew.
                                    Mixed demographics to represent diverse user perspectives,
                                    with no prior relationship to Family Promise (unbiased
                                    mental models).
                                </p>
                                <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 italic">
                                    Participants created between 4 and 7 groups
                                    each, revealing diverse mental models while
                                    showing underlying patterns.
                                </p>
                            </div>

                            <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-8 shadow-lg">
                                <div
                                    class="text-3xl font-black number-badge mb-4"
                                >
                                    03
                                </div>
                                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">
                                    Session Design
                                </h3>
                                <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
                                    I wrote a facilitation script to ensure
                                    consistency across sessions. Participants
                                    grouped cards in ways that made sense to
                                    them while using "think aloud" protocol to
                                    capture their reasoning.
                                </p>
                            </div>

                            <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-8 shadow-lg">
                                <div
                                    class="text-3xl font-black number-badge mb-4"
                                >
                                    04
                                </div>
                                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">
                                    Cross-Disciplinary Collaboration
                                </h3>
                                <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
                                    I trained developer Matthew to facilitate
                                    sessions alongside me, doubling our capacity
                                    and exposing him to UX research methods.
                                    This reinforced the value of
                                    cross-functional partnership.
                                </p>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="image-float">
                            <img
                                src="/fp-cardsort.webp"
                                alt="Card sorting session in FigJam"
                                class="w-full rounded-xl shadow-lg"
                            />
                            <p class="text-center text-gray-500 mt-4 text-sm">
                                Remote card sorting sessions conducted via
                                FigJam
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Data Analysis -->
                    <div class="mb-32 scroll-reveal">
                        <h2
                            class="text-5xl md:text-6xl font-black mb-16 leading-tight"
                        >
                            Data Analysis
                        </h2>

                        <div
                            class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-12 md:p-16 shadow-xl mb-12"
                        >
                            <span
                                class="inline-block bg-orange-100 text-orange-700 px-4 py-2 rounded-full text-sm font-medium mb-6"
                                >The Challenge</span
                            >
                            <h3 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">
                                From Overwhelm to Insight
                            </h3>
                            <p
                                class="text-xl text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-6"
                            >
                                After 10 sessions, I had 10 completely different
                                card groupings. Some participants created 4
                                categories. Others created 7. Card labels varied
                                wildly ("Help" vs. "Get Support" vs.
                                "Services").
                            </p>
                            <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">
                                The question: How do you identify patterns in
                                this chaos?
                            </p>
                        </div>

                        <h3 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-8">
                            The Solution: Data Visualization
                        </h3>

                        <div class="space-y-8 mb-16">
                            <div class="bg-blue-50 rounded-xl p-8">
                                <h4 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">
                                    1. Data Compilation
                                </h4>
                                <p
                                    class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"
                                >
                                    I compiled the card sort data into a
                                    structured spreadsheet, tracking which cards
                                    each participant grouped together across all
                                    10 sessions. This raw data became the
                                    foundation for generating visualizations
                                    that would reveal patterns.
                                </p>
                            </div>

                            <div class="bg-blue-50 rounded-xl p-8">
                                <h4 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">
                                    2. Custom Python Scripts
                                </h4>
                                <p
                                    class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4"
                                >
                                    I researched hierarchical clustering methods
                                    and wrote Python scripts (with ChatGPT
                                    assistance) that transformed my data into
                                    visual formats:
                                </p>
                                <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-700">
                                    <li class="flex items-start">
                                        <span class="text-blue-600 mr-3 text-xl"
                                            >📊</span
                                        >
                                        <div>
                                            <strong
                                                >Dendrogram (Tree Diagram):</strong
                                            > Shows hierarchical relationships between
                                            cards, reveals which content naturally
                                            "belongs together"
                                        </div>
                                    </li>
                                    <li class="flex items-start">
                                        <span class="text-blue-600 mr-3 text-xl"
                                            >🗺️</span
                                        >
                                        <div>
                                            <strong>Heat Map:</strong> Color-coded
                                            matrix showing co-occurrence frequency—darker
                                            colors indicate stronger relationships
                                        </div>
                                    </li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <!-- Interactive Visualizations - FIXED SPACING -->
                        <div class="mb-20">
                            <div
                                class="bg-gradient-to-br from-blue-700 to-cyan-700 text-white rounded-2xl p-12 mb-16"
                            >
                                <h3 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">
                                    Interactive Visualizations
                                </h3>
                                <p class="text-xl opacity-90 mb-4">
                                    The dendrogram and heat map below are fully
                                    interactive. Click to explore the data and
                                    see how participants grouped content.
                                </p>
                                <p class="text-lg opacity-80">
                                    Note: Opens in new tab for full-screen
                                    interactive experience
                                </p>
                            </div>

                            <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12">
                                <!-- Dendrogram Card -->
                                <a
                                    href="/dendrogram.html"
                                    target="_blank"
                                    class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-xl hover:shadow-2xl transition-all duration-300 overflow-hidden group"
                                >
                                    <div class="p-4">
                                        <img
                                            src="/dendrogram.png"
                                            alt="Interactive dendrogram visualization"
                                            class="w-full rounded-lg"
                                        />
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="p-8">
                                        <h4
                                            class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 group-hover:text-blue-600 transition"
                                        >
                                            Interactive Dendrogram
                                        </h4>
                                        <p
                                            class="text-gray-600 text-lg mb-6 leading-relaxed"
                                        >
                                            Explore the hierarchical clustering
                                            of card sort data
                                        </p>
                                        <span
                                            class="inline-flex items-center text-blue-600 font-bold text-lg group-hover:gap-3 transition-all"
                                        >
                                            Open Interactive View
                                            <svg
                                                class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform"
                                                fill="none"
                                                stroke="currentColor"
                                                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                                            >
                                                <path
                                                    stroke-linecap="round"
                                                    stroke-linejoin="round"
                                                    stroke-width="2"
                                                    d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3"
                                                ></path>
                                            </svg>
                                        </span>
                                    </div>
                                </a>

                                <!-- Heat Map Card -->
                                <a
                                    href="/heatmap.html"
                                    target="_blank"
                                    class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-xl hover:shadow-2xl transition-all duration-300 overflow-hidden group"
                                >
                                    <div class="p-4">
                                        <img
                                            src="/heatmap.png"
                                            alt="Interactive heat map visualization"
                                            class="w-full rounded-lg"
                                        />
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="p-8">
                                        <h4
                                            class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 group-hover:text-blue-600 transition"
                                        >
                                            Interactive Heat Map
                                        </h4>
                                        <p
                                            class="text-gray-600 text-lg mb-6 leading-relaxed"
                                        >
                                            See co-occurrence patterns across
                                            participants
                                        </p>
                                        <span
                                            class="inline-flex items-center text-blue-600 font-bold text-lg group-hover:gap-3 transition-all"
                                        >
                                            Open Interactive View
                                            <svg
                                                class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform"
                                                fill="none"
                                                stroke="currentColor"
                                                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                                            >
                                                <path
                                                    stroke-linecap="round"
                                                    stroke-linejoin="round"
                                                    stroke-width="2"
                                                    d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3"
                                                ></path>
                                            </svg>
                                        </span>
                                    </div>
                                </a>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="bg-green-50 rounded-xl p-8">
                            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">
                                Pattern Identification
                            </h3>
                            <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6">
                                The visualizations revealed clear clusters:
                            </p>
                            <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-700">
                                <li class="flex items-start">
                                    <span class="text-green-600 mr-2">✓</span>
                                    <span
                                        ><strong>"Who We Are"</strong> content (Our
                                        Story, Our Impact, Our History, Staff and
                                        Board) formed a tight cluster—validating that
                                        users saw these as variations of the same
                                        information need</span
                                    >
                                </li>
                                <li class="flex items-start">
                                    <span class="text-green-600 mr-2">✓</span>
                                    <span
                                        ><strong>"What We Do"</strong> (program information,
                                        homelessness context) grouped together</span
                                    >
                                </li>
                                <li class="flex items-start">
                                    <span class="text-green-600 mr-2">✓</span>
                                    <span
                                        ><strong>Resources and Help</strong> formed
                                        their own distinct area</span
                                    >
                                </li>
                                <li class="flex items-start">
                                    <span class="text-green-600 mr-2">✓</span>
                                    <span
                                        ><strong>Get Involved actions</strong> (Donate,
                                        Volunteer, Contact) clustered as a separate
                                        engagement category</span
                                    >
                                </li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Design Solution -->
                    <div class="mb-32 scroll-reveal">
                        <h2
                            class="text-5xl md:text-6xl font-black mb-16 leading-tight"
                        >
                            Translating<br />Insights into Design
                        </h2>

                        <div class="bg-blue-50 rounded-xl p-8 mb-12">
                            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">
                                The Dendrogram-to-Sitemap Process
                            </h3>
                            <p
                                class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-6"
                            >
                                The dendrogram provided structure, but <strong
                                    >data doesn't dictate design</strong
                                >—it informs it. I adapted the clusters based
                                on:
                            </p>
                            <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-700">
                                <li class="flex items-start">
                                    <span class="text-blue-600 mr-3">•</span>
                                    <span
                                        ><strong>User Priorities:</strong> Families
                                        in crisis need immediate access to help</span
                                    >
                                </li>
                                <li class="flex items-start">
                                    <span class="text-blue-600 mr-3">•</span>
                                    <span
                                        ><strong>Business Goals:</strong> Nonprofit
                                        sustainability requires visible donation pathways</span
                                    >
                                </li>
                                <li class="flex items-start">
                                    <span class="text-blue-600 mr-3">•</span>
                                    <span
                                        ><strong>Content Strategy:</strong> Merge
                                        redundant pages, eliminate outdated content</span
                                    >
